# A containment cycle need not be one hop. Neither record names itself, but
# each holds the other BY VALUE, so neither has a size and neither can lay out.
#
# The check that finds it asks whether the target is on the CONTAINMENT path --
# the chain of field and arm typerefs open above it. Asking instead whether the
# target is merely mid-resolution caught this one by accident (the grey mark is
# set for every edge, so the one-hop case happened to line up) and reported a
# cycle for types that only appeared in a method signature on the way past.
Aa: record { b: Bb }
Bb: record { a: Aa }

main: function is {
    x: (Aa b: (Bb a: (Aa b: (Bb a: 0))))
    print "x"
}
